   "answer": "On this Linux worktree the vendor Claude CLI and ~/.claude are absent, so the map is measured against a throwaway --settings home driven by command-center/p2-wave/probes/RES-0018/lifecycle.py (not a Windows live profile). Isolation from a sibling live home is proven before the first command (distinct paths, disjoint isolation markers, live census unchanged through the cycle). Per-command filesystem diffs (hash_census) are: install files=10 keys=6, update files=15 keys=2, repair files=1 keys=0, rollback files=5 keys=2, uninstall files=20 keys=6. Winning enablement key is settings.json enabledPlugins; .claude.json never received that key. Clean uninstall removes installed payload, cache, rollback store, inventory row and the enabledPlugins entry; a subsequent install does not inherit the prior-state marker (verdict=NO_INHERIT). Naive uninstall that leaves cache DOES inherit — the detector is not silent in both states. SUCCESS:RES-0018 in the receipt AND a per-command filesystem diff from a provably isolated throwaway profile plus an orphan verdict",
